                    {
                        "form_id": "4e5f72e4-b943-4154-9f7d-6baa7afe5d17",
                        "entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "панеги́рике"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "726ff0a6-52c8-4f2f-82a6-7d53385aaf9c",
                        "entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "панеги́риках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a3ffa19-29ec-37c8-9981-d4b34f8c2516",
                        "entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. ораторская хвалебная речь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d46be1f-fa57-4507-99f5-51208b1e23a4",
                                "sense_id": "5a3ffa19-29ec-37c8-9981-d4b34f8c2516",
                                "text": "В народе раздавались восторженные крики, слышались мольбы за Хмельницкого; духовенство, академия вышли к нему навстречу, профессора говорили панегирики, называли Хмельницкого Моисеем веры русской, защитником свободы русского народа, новым Маккавеем."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbe8245b-6a28-460a-ac4e-bd2d9acbda93",
                                "sense_id": "5a3ffa19-29ec-37c8-9981-d4b34f8c2516",
                                "text": "Наш редактор только покачивал молча головой и хладнокровно вымарывал его панегирики."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21f6a7ac-ac61-3b1d-97a8-51e6942c5f7b",
                        "entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., книжн., неодобр. восторженная, неумеренная похвала"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "015e4092-bad4-42a4-8182-20d76e1f049e",
                                "sense_id": "21f6a7ac-ac61-3b1d-97a8-51e6942c5f7b",
                                "text": "Однако всё чаще защита друзей сбивается на панегирик, на обвинения тем, кто осмелился о Карамзине толковать без должного почтения."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a9238313-c48b-46db-8d97-f8ac114d7dbf",
                        "source_entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "source_sense_description": "жанр",
                        "target_lang_word": "panegyric",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "panegyric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4dc47dbd-6fbd-358f-b388-5258dc21ec72",
                                        "entry_id": "e9f6b407-b01d-326a-b5bd-a3a5a04d9cca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A formal speech publicly praising someone or something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd16804a-6135-4f1e-a827-900f350a7c35",
                                                "sense_id": "4dc47dbd-6fbd-358f-b388-5258dc21ec72",
                                                "text": "My little Friend Grildrig, you have made a moſt admirable Panegyrick upon your Country: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28a8ccc6-82b8-4ba6-890c-df1965532842",
                                                "sense_id": "4dc47dbd-6fbd-358f-b388-5258dc21ec72",
                                                "text": "Want of something else to say, and a very shady lane, disposed him to confidence; and he forthwith began a panegyric on himself, and on the good fortune of Miss Arundel, stating, he was now on his road to offer himself and his debts to her acceptance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11c47b17-f6db-40cd-bf3c-06dae617db4d",
                                                "sense_id": "4dc47dbd-6fbd-358f-b388-5258dc21ec72",
                                                "text": "The painter's absurd fits of jealousy, his wild devotion, his extravagant panegyrics, his curious reticences—he understood them all now, and he felt sorry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fd18d65-51e3-4352-8480-b901a57e9e12",
                                                "sense_id": "4dc47dbd-6fbd-358f-b388-5258dc21ec72",
                                                "text": "He then spoke in the usual boastful manner of his progenitors, added a flaming panegyric upon himself, and strolled down the road to repeat his speech at the next house."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59c05215-52af-4ae0-9653-9688e5640b52",
                                                "sense_id": "4dc47dbd-6fbd-358f-b388-5258dc21ec72",
                                                "text": "Another manifestation, significantly reaching its apogee in the midst of Antonine virtues, was the growing popularity of adoxographical exercises. Mock panegyrics were dashed off, not just by sardonic intellectuals such as Lucian, but also by trained courtiers and polished encomiasts of the stamp of [Marcus Cornelius] Fronto."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "778e99bb-c94b-3594-bd15-442380a0fb6d",
                                        "entry_id": "e9f6b407-b01d-326a-b5bd-a3a5a04d9cca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who writes or delivers such a speech."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "panegyric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a171c253-206f-3b2e-b880-fab6a94dd2a6",
                                        "entry_id": "833571dd-3136-3713-95f1-fc63163f8a62",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "panegyrical"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b2121cca-f560-451b-b9d2-948baa168d6c",
                        "source_entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "source_sense_description": "жанр",
                        "target_lang_word": "eulogy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eulogy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "360cfd4c-13b8-3749-bb69-7549a0dad7dc",
                                        "entry_id": "a1471620-5caf-39aa-8aa0-56efa47e833d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An oration to honor a deceased person, usually at a funeral."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a300d9f6-25e2-3ed1-a5fe-594e391d960a",
                                        "entry_id": "a1471620-5caf-39aa-8aa0-56efa47e833d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Speaking highly of someone or something; the act of praising or commending someone or something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08b2e960-8f07-48c8-9e89-651f10796d32",
                                                "sense_id": "a300d9f6-25e2-3ed1-a5fe-594e391d960a",
                                                "text": "It was the prettiest and most luxurious little sitting-room I had ever seen; and I admired it with the warmest enthusiasm. The solemn servant was far too highly trained to betray the slightest satisfaction. He bowed with icy deference when my terms of eulogy were all exhausted, and silently opened the door for me to go out into the passage again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d54f5940-6128-422e-b028-804043775fb3",
                                                "sense_id": "a300d9f6-25e2-3ed1-a5fe-594e391d960a",
                                                "text": "The Southampton striker, who also struck a post late on, was being serenaded by the Wembley crowd before the end and should probably brace himself for some Lambert-mania over the coming days but, amid the eulogies, it should not overlook the deficiencies that were evident in another stodgy England performance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ff729c8-99f2-41e9-9b07-bf3741f97deb",
                        "source_entry_id": "674d86ea-ffed-3d20-baee-232d65b4aa46",
                        "source_sense_description": "жанр",
                        "target_lang_word": "panegiryk",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "panegiryk",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93237870-f187-3269-9bd6-b0123088c970",
                                        "entry_id": "c6a55c82-db27-3870-bd26-11940c7bf253",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "uroczysty tekst pochwalny, sławiący konkretną osobę, czyn"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9a75ec3-d9f7-4ea3-84ed-b7415b38f83a",
                                                "sense_id": "93237870-f187-3269-9bd6-b0123088c970",
                                                "text": "Kałużyńskiemu co prawda zdarzało się pisać chwalebne panegiryki pod adresem sztuki doby komunizmu, ale po latach potrafił przyznać się do błędu, czego nie można powiedzieć o wielu jego młodszy kolegach."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
